Opening message: 
Welcome, everyone, and thanks for being here! I’m ___ , and joining me are___ ,____  and ___. Together, we’ll be guiding you through today’s exercise. You’ll be stepping into the role of the incident response team at SimCorp, a fictional company that’s been hit by a cyber incident. Your job is to work together, assess the situation, and respond as the incident unfolds.
Before we jump in, here’s a quick overview of how the day will run. The exercise will last 2 hours and 50 minutes in total. We’ll start with a 15-minute briefing, where I’ll walk you through everything you need to know before we begin. Then, we’ll move into 2 hours and 10 minutes of gameplay, which officially starts when the first message from SimCorp comes through. We’ll wrap up with a 25-minute debrief to reflect on what happened, discuss what went well, and identify what you might do differently next time.
Throughout the exercise, you’ll be working as a team, so communication is key. Share information, talk through your findings, and make decisions together. If you find yourselves stuck at any point, you can also ask for a hint. I’ll explain how that works as part of the briefing. Over the next 15 minutes, we’ll cover the ground rules, give you some background on SimCorp, walk through how to access your tools, and explain what you’ll need to submit by the end of the exercise.
With that, let’s get started!

